  "name": "DJ Assault",
  "editorial_article": "Craig De Shan Adams, born in 1977, established his career as a Detroit-based electronic producer who pioneered the booty music and ghettotech genres. Starting his DJ practice at age 12, Adams drew from the radio broadcasts of the Electrifying Mojo on WMXD and later integrated influences from the Atlanta bass scene during his college years. He rose to international attention in the mid-1990s through singles such as 'Sex on the Beach' and 'Ass and Titties,' released alongside producer Mr. De' on labels like Electrofunk and Assault Rifle. Adams founded the label Jefferson Ave in the mid-2000s to self-release his projects. Known for his comedic and sexually explicit lyrical style, he has cited Jeff Mills, Farley Jackmaster Funk, and Bad Boy Bill as core influences on his musical output.",
